<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 755 million zlotys against a 1.1 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold T-bills worth 710 million zlotys.</p>
<p>It will offer 1.2 billion zlotys worth of bills at its next primary auction on July 7.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    13-week  26-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price   94.93    90.14    81.96</p>
<p>(pvs auction)  (94.95)  (90.17)  (82.04)</p>
<p>   new max price   95.00    90.23    83.04</p>
<p>(pvs auction)  (95.10)  (90.30)  (82.16)</p>
<p>   offer	     200.0    200.0    700.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded   210.1    101.1    444.0</p>
<p>   bids accepted   204.1     95.1    411.0</p>
<p>   next auction    200.0    300.0    700.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
